Declare a String named myString set to "SEPTEMBER", then store the index of the first \'E\' in an int named first.', 10, 1, '{"tile_elevations": {}}', 10, 0.78000000, 1, 8, 'String myString = "SEPTEMBER"; int first = myString.indexOf(\'E\');', '[{"part": "String myString = \\"SEPTEMBER\\";", "explanation": "The string to search."}, {"part": "int first", "explanation": "An int variable, because indexOf() returns an index."}, {"part": "myString.indexOf(\'E\')", "explanation": "Finds the first E and returns its index, which is 1."}, {"part": ";", "explanation": "Ends the statement."}]'),
(184, 6, 'Level 6', 'STRINGS AND DECISIONS', 'The Missing Word', 'indexOf also works with a whole piece of text. The indexOf(aSubString) method returns the first occurrence of aSubString in myString, or, in its absence, returns -1. There is also indexOf(aSubString, beginIndex), which begins the search at beginIndex. In "SEPTEMBER", the substring "EM" is found at index 4, but "XYZ" is not there at all.

Declare a String named myString set to "SEPTEMBER", then store the result of searching for "XYZ" in an int named missing.', 'A substring goes in double quotes. The result will be -1.', 'String myString = "SEPTEMBER"; int missing = myString.indexOf("XYZ");', 50, 8, 6, 1, '2026-10-10 08:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 'Use the exact solution: String myString = "SEPTEMBER"; int missing = myString.indexOf("XYZ");', 'String\\s+myString\\s+=\\s+"SEPTEMBER";\\s+int\\s+missing\\s+=\\s+myString\\.indexOf\\(\\s*"XYZ"\\s*\\);', '/assets/landscapes/oakheart2.png', 'indexOf() With a Substring', 'indexOf also works with a whole piece of text. The indexOf(aSubString) method returns the first occurrence of aSubString in myString, or, in its absence, returns -1. There is also indexOf(aSubString, beginIndex), which begins the search at beginIndex. In "SEPTEMBER", the substring "EM" is found at index 4, but "XYZ" is not there at all.

Declare a String named myString set to "SEPTEMBER", then store the result of searching for "XYZ" in an int named missing.', 10, 1, '{"tile_elevations": {}}', 10, 0.78000000, 1, 8, 'String myString = "SEPTEMBER"; int missing = myString.indexOf("XYZ");', '[{"part": "String myString = \\"SEPTEMBER\\";", "explanation": "The string to search."}, {"part": "int missing", "explanation": "Holds the index that indexOf() returns."}, {"part": "myString.indexOf(\\"XYZ\\")", "explanation": "Searches for the text XYZ. It is absent, so the result is -1."}, {"part": ";", "explanation": "Ends the statement."}]'),
